{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he shall bring his guilt-offering to HaShem for his sin which he sinned, a female, etc.</b> The Sages of blessed memory called this passage קרבן עולה ויורד — 'the ascending and descending offering.' The meaning of אשמו is 'his offering,' and it was not an אשם (guilt-offering) but rather a חטאת (sin-offering), as it says, ״a female from the flock, a lamb or a she-goat, for a sin-offering.״ And the offering is called by the term אשם because the אשם (guilt) is the cause of the offering, just as Scripture calls wisdom לב (heart) because the heart is the cause of wisdom, for thought and wisdom reside in the heart." "<b>And know</b> that the reason the Sages called these offerings קרבן עולה ויורד — 'the ascending and descending offering' — is that if a person was rich at the time of his sin and afterward became poor, he brings the offering of the poor; if he became rich again, he brings the offering of the rich. Therefore they called it קרבן עולה ויורד. The offering of the rich is a female lamb or a she-goat for a sin-offering; the offering of the poor is תורים ובני יונה (turtledoves or young pigeons); the offering of the poorest of the poor is a tenth of an ephah. And the Sages of blessed memory received that the value of the lamb or the she-goat, which is the offering of the rich, is two shekels, in the manner written regarding the ram (Leviticus 5): ״בערכך כסף שקלים בשקל הקדש לאשם״ — 'in your valuation, silver shekels, by the holy shekel, for the guilt-offering' — and the minimum of 'shekels' is two, and he must bring an offering whose value is at least two shekels. And these two shekels are ten Arabian shekels. And the offering of the poor, which is תורים ובני יונה, its value is a tenth of the value of the animal. And the offering of the poorest of the poor, which is a tenth of an ephah, its value is a tenth of the value of the תורים ובני יונה. And this is why you find עשירת האפה written defectively (without a יו״ד), alluding to the measure of these three offerings."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:23:30.659916492Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}